data: {"type": "thinking", "id": "t4", "content": "The analysis is clear. Now let me write the final output document with the findings and prioritized copy changes.\n\nLet me think about what specific headline/subheadline rewrites I should recommend:\n\n**Current headline:** \"The intelligent marketing system\"\n**Current subheadline:** \"DOJO watches every channel, tracks your brand, runs your workflows, and acts before you have to. Getting smarter every time.\"\n\n**The gap:**\n1. Buyers are searching for \"marketing intelligence\" (not \"intelligent marketing\") - word order and framing matters\n2. Buyers are searching for \"platform\" and \"software\" labels - DOJO uses \"system\" which is less recognized\n\n\n3. \"Marketing analytics\" and \"unified marketing analytics\" are buyer search terms that aren't reflected in the current copy\n4. The word \"automation\" drives 34+ conversions but doesn't appear in the headline area, despite being central to marketing automation platform searches\n5. \"B2B\" is a qualifier buyers use when searching but isn't present in the copy\n6. \"Marketing operations\" is a converting term that's missing from the messaging\n\nFor the headline, I'm recommending we shift to \"The marketing intelligence platform\" to align directly with top converting search terms, or alternatively \"Marketing intelligence, built for the whole stack\" to capture the broader scope.\n\nThe subheadline needs to explicitly include \"marketing intelligence\" and use \"platform\" or \"software\" language while keeping the benefit-focused messaging. Section labels should swap \"Proactive Dashboard\" for something incorporating \"unified analytics\" or \"marketing analytics,\" and we need to work \"marketing automation\" into the copy somewhere.\n\nThe meta description should feature \"marketing intelligence platform\" or \"marketing intelligence software\" prominently.\n\nI'm noticing there's a real tension here between the deliberate brand positioning of \"intelligent marketing system\" and what buyers are actually searching for, so the recommendations should acknowledge that trade-off and suggest ways to bridge both."}

