data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a7", "content": "\n\nThe three dominant buyer categories are: **\"marketing intelligence\"** (300 conversions), **\"platform/software\"** (a label buyers expect), and **\"automation\"** (38+ conversions). None appear in the headline or subheadline.\n\n### Gap 2: Homepage language that buyers never use\n\nEvery one of these phrases appears prominently on the page and in zero search queries:\n\n- \"compounding intelligence\" (section header)\n- \"living graph\" (feature section)\n- \"proactive agents\" (feature section)\n- \"always on-capture\" (section label)\n- **\"intelligent marketing system\" (the main headline)**\n\nThe headline itself is the most critical miss. \"Marketing intelligence\" is a recognized software category buyers search by name. \"Intelligent marketing system\" is DOJO's framing of itself — word order and all. Those are not the same thing, and Google treats them differently.\n\n### Gap 3: Positioning fragmentation between organic and paid\n\nDOJO ranks organically for \"marketing OS / marketing operating system\" (35 + 25 clicks at positions 6 and 5.6) but that category barely converts in paid. The converting category is \"marketing intelligence platform\" — where DOJO has almost no organic presence yet. The homepage needs to bridge these or commit.\n\n---\n\n## The 6 Prioritized Changes\n\n| Priority | Change | Conversion signal |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🔴 P0 | Rewrite main headline | 300 conversions on matching terms |\n| 🔴 P0 | Rewrite subheadline | 417 conversions across all gaps |\n| 🔴 P0 | Update meta title + description | Same + SEO CTR impact |\n| 🟠 P1 | Rename \"Proactive Dashboard\" → \"Unified Marketing Analytics\" | 11 conversions |\n| 🟠 P1 | Rename \"Pre-Built Workflows\" → \"Marketing Workflow Automation\" | 38 conversions in automation cluster |\n| 🟠 P1 | Add B2B qualifier in hero | 34 conversions |\n\n**Specific rewrites are in the output file** — including two headline options that preserve DOJO's differentiation while front-loading buyer language.\n\nThe full analysis is saved. Want to go deeper on any of the three \"Going Deeper\" paths: landing page extension (pricing/product page), competitor language validation, or an A/B test brief?"}
